==== stdout ====
Usage: raphael search <path>... -q <query> [options]
       raphael search --id <id> -q <query> [options]

Search all descendants by text.

Search is recursive by default; use --direct for direct children only. Search
everything with `raphael search / -q auth`. Matching includes titles,
descriptions and note text. Repeat -q to OR queries together, at most 10
queries. Each query allows at most 1000 characters and 32 words or quoted
phrases. Words separated by spaces mean OR; uppercase AND binds more tightly
than uppercase OR. Double quotes make a phrase. Words joined by punctuation,
such as auth-token or auth.token, must appear together and in that order, like a
phrase. * is punctuation too: auth* matches auth, not authentication. Operators
need a word or phrase on both sides. Lowercase and and or are ordinary search
words. There are no parentheses, NOT, wildcards or field prefixes. Matching
ignores case and accents; there is no stemming: token does not match tokens.

Results are ordered by relevance; --order-by is not accepted.

Rules:
  The default page contains at most 50 results. --limit accepts 1–500; --skip
    skips results. At most 10 paths or ids may be searched or listed in one
    request.
  --filter accepts a JSON object with keys type, kind, tags. Allowed type
    values: area, project, resource. Allowed kind values: note. Each value is a
    scalar or {"$in":[...]}; sibling keys are ANDed. Tags match at least one
    supplied tag, with exact case after trimming and NFC normalization. A kind
    does not imply a type.
  A value that starts with -, such as a query, must be joined to its flag with
    =, as in `--query=-draft`; otherwise it is read as another option and
    refused.

Options:
      --id <id>
          Include this id alongside positional paths. Repeatable.
      --filter <json|@file>
          JSON object. Keys: type, kind, tags. Values may use {"$in":[...]}. See
          `raphael help addressing`.
      --skip <n>
          Number of results to skip. Default: 0.
      --limit <n>
          Page size, 1 to 500. Default: 50.
      --include-archived
          Include archived items.
  -q, --query <text>
          Text to search. At least one required. Repeatable.
      --direct
          Search direct children only.
      --json
          Print the result as one JSON document.
  -h, --help
          Show help.

Examples:
  raphael search / -q auth
  raphael search /work -q '"login flow" AND retry'
  raphael search /work /personal -q auth --limit 20
  raphael search /work --direct -q auth --filter '{"type":"resource","kind":"note"}'

Prints:
  One row per match, closest first: id, type, state, path, title. JSON carries
  `items[].node` and `page`.

Next: raphael get --id 42

See also: raphael help addressing; raphael help output
